\ul\b 03-RENEWABLE ENERGY AND ENVIRONMENTAL ISSUES :\par
\ulnone\b0 Date: 1 Nov 2023\par
Time: 01:00 PM - 3:30 PM\par
Location: ENSIT\par
Attendees: 32 (30 IEEE members, 2 non-IEEE members)\par
An enlightening workshop on renewable energy and environmental\par
challenges took place, uniting experts and enthusiasts to explore\par
sustainable solutions. The event featured presentations by Saif\par
Dormek and Takoua Yahyaoui.\par
Saif discussed the critical impacts of environmental degradation, such\par
as climate change and pollution, emphasizing the importance of\par
research to address these issues. He proposed innovative and\par
economical approaches for mitigation.\par
Following Saif\rquote s insightful discourse, Takoua delved into renewable\par
energy, focusing on photovoltaics. She explained how solar cells work\par
and highlighted Tunisia's plans to increase the use of renewable\par
energy, aiming to reduce fossil fuel dependency and promote\par
sustainability.\par
The workshop offered valuable insights into tackling environmental\par
challenges and advancing renewable energy, underscoring the need\par
for ongoing research and practical solutions.\par
